# Debounce vs throttle

Both tame a noisy event stream, but they answer different questions.
Debounce answers "has the user stopped?"; it waits for a quiet gap
before firing.

```ts
function debounce<A extends unknown[]>(
  fn: (...args: A) => void,
  waitMs: number
): (...args: A) => void {
  let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), waitMs);
  };
}
```

Every call resets the timer, so `fn` runs once, `waitMs` after the
last call. A search box uses this: no request per keystroke, one
request when typing pauses.
